Page Sections (top to bottom in index.html)





Navbar -- Logo text ("DigiCraft"), nav links (Services, Industries, Why Us, Process, Contact), sticky on scroll



Hero -- Headline, subheadline, two CTA buttons (WhatsApp chat link, consultation anchor to contact form), subtle gradient mesh background



Services -- 3-card grid (Website Dev, Business Automation, Mobile App Dev) with icon, title, bullet list



Portfolio / Proof of Work -- Showcase grid with 4-6 mock project cards (screenshots described via CSS gradient placeholders), project name, category tag, brief description. Builds trust without needing real images.



Who We Work With -- 8-item icon grid (Clinics, Schools, Salons, Gyms, Real Estate, Restaurants, Retail, Service Providers) with CSS-only icons via Unicode/emoji



Why Choose Us -- 5-item feature list with checkmark icons and short descriptions



Process -- 4-step horizontal timeline (Consultation, Planning & Design, Development, Launch & Support)



CTA Banner -- "Ready to Build Your Online Presence?" with "Start Your Project Today" button



Contact -- Two-column layout: left = form (Name, Business Name, Phone, Message + submit), right = email + WhatsApp click-to-chat link + embedded Google Maps placeholder



Footer -- Centered copyright line "© 2026 All Rights Reserved"



Floating WhatsApp Button -- Fixed bottom-right, green circle with WhatsApp icon (SVG inline), links to https://wa.me/918920842499

Key Design Decisions





No images required -- All visuals via CSS gradients, SVG icons, and Unicode symbols. Portfolio cards use styled gradient placeholders with overlay text.



Color palette: White #FFFFFF, Light gray #F8FAFC, Blue accent #2563EB, Dark text #0F172A, Muted text #64748B



Typography: Inter font, sizes from 1rem (body) to 3.5rem (hero headline), generous line-height



Animations: Intersection Observer-based fade-in-up on scroll for each section



Contact form: Posts to https://formsubmit.co/guptaaryan583@gmail.com (free, no backend needed) or shows a success message via JS



Mobile: Hamburger menu toggle, single-column stacked layout, touch-friendly tap targets

